<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n18305" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄφθεγκ-τος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄφθογγος</span>
			, <i>voiceless,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μηνυτήρ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.
					<u>Eu.</u>
					245
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">στόμα</span> (of a pen) <i><span class="en">
				<u>AP</u>
				9.162
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀστράγαλοι</span> ib.<i><span class="en">
				7.427.14
			</span></i> (Antip. Sid.). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			of places, etc., <i>where none may speak,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τῷδ᾽ ἐν ἀφθέγκτῳ νάπει</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					S.
					<u>OC</u>
					156
				</span></i>
			 (lyr.). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			
				Pass.
			, <i>unspeakable, unutterable,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				B.
				<u>Fr.</u>
				2.2
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Sph.</u>
				238c
			</span></i>. Adv.
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-τως</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Iamb.
					<u>Myst.</u>
					7.4
				</span></i>
			.</div>
